# Who must review what.
#
# The rule this file encodes: *code* needs a maintainer's eyes, *labels* do not.
#
# Every contributor runs app/server.py and scripts/bounty.py on their own machine
# with their own GitHub token, so merging code is equivalent to running it for
# them. That is the trust boundary this file protects.
#
# Deliberately absent: data/datasets/*/labels/**. Labels are data, they are the
# whole point of a bounty PR, and requiring review there would make bounties
# unshippable. GitHub skips the "require code owner review" check when a PR
# touches no owned path, which is exactly the behaviour wanted for label PRs.

# --- everything that executes ------------------------------------------------
/app/                    @MicahHeneveld
/scripts/                @MicahHeneveld
/notebooks/              @MicahHeneveld
/configs/                @MicahHeneveld
/.github/                @MicahHeneveld
/requirements.txt        @MicahHeneveld

# --- build and container definitions ----------------------------------------
Dockerfile               @MicahHeneveld
docker-compose.yml       @MicahHeneveld

# --- data that is *not* a label --------------------------------------------
# Labels are the only dataset files a reviewer writes, so everything else in a
# dataset still needs review: data.yaml drives split paths, manifest.json drives
# ingest bookkeeping, and predictions feed the disagreement overlay.
/data/datasets/*/data.yaml        @MicahHeneveld
/data/datasets/*/manifest.json    @MicahHeneveld
/data/datasets/*/frames.csv       @MicahHeneveld
/data/datasets/*/predictions/     @MicahHeneveld

# --- docs ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Inert: rendered, never executed.
/docs/                   @MicahHeneveld
*.md                     @MicahHeneveld
